-- title:
--   Frobenius-fixed elements detect the exponent v modulo d
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a natural number, prime by hypothesis, let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring and $\pi \in \mathcal{O}$. Let $O^{nr}$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, and let $\mathrm{Fr}$ be an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism of $O^{nr}$. Write $\mathfrak{m}$ for the ideal of $O^{nr}$ generated by the image of $\pi$ under the structure map. Assume: $O^{nr}$ is $\mathfrak{m}$-adically complete; $\mathfrak{m}$ is maximal; every monic polynomial over $O^{nr}$ of positive degree has an element of $O^{nr}$ at which its value lies in $\mathfrak{m}$ (so the residue field $O^{nr}/\mathfrak{m}$ is algebraically closed); $\mathrm{Fr}(x) - x^{r} \in \mathfrak{m}$ for all $x \in O^{nr}$; and $r \in \mathfrak{m}$. Let $k$ be a field and $\psi : O^{nr} \to k$ a ring homomorphism killing the image of $\pi$. Let $d$ be a positive natural number and $v$ an integer, and suppose that for every $y \in O^{nr}$ fixed by the integer power $\mathrm{Fr}^{d}$ one has $\psi(\mathrm{Fr}^{-v} y) = \psi(y)$, the powers being taken in the automorphism group. Then $d \mid v$ in $\mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   This is the rigidity statement that a power of Frobenius acting trivially, after reduction along $\psi$, on the elements of the unramified ring fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^{d}$ must have exponent divisible by $d$; the Teichmüller representatives of the degree-$d$ subfield of the residue field provide the witnesses. It is used in the Cherednik–Drinfeld rigidification step, where a Frobenius twist of a point datum has to be identified with the untwisted one.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Int_natCast_dvd_of_forall_frobeniusLift_pow_fixed_apply_zpow_eq.lean

